<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maba Diakhou Ba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1809–1867</span> · Also known as Maba Jaxu Ba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maba Diakhou Ba was a Muslim cleric and leader of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegambia">Senegambia</a> region in the 1860s. From his base in Rip he conquered much of the Kingdom of Saloum and spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolof">Wolof</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serer">Serer</a>, resisting both traditional rulers and the French. He invaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-sine">Kingdom of Sine</a>, but was defeated and killed at the battle of Fandane-Thiouthioune in 1867.</p></div>
